{"t":1792696463,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"34e66985-3fbe-4943-9351-cfd30c97f3d4","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-10-22T18:58:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 221858\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n258 PM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nTidal flooding issues will continue into the weekend, with some\nheadlines being extended. Check the latest CFW for updates. \n\nSmall Craft Advisories were extended into Friday, see the marine\nforecast discussion below for details. \n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Dry and seasonable conditions continue through early next\n  week, with frost possible this weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and seasonable conditions continue through \nearly next week, with frost possible this weekend.\n\nSurface high pressure remains to the north through Saturday with\ndry and seasonable conditions expected to continue. High \ntemperatures today will be in the 60s for most with only highest\nelevations staying in the 50s. Tonight, low temperatures will \nbe in the upper 30s to 40s. For Friday and Saturday, surface \nhigh pressure extends southward from Canada with dry cold fronts\nbringing in cooler air. High temperatures stay in the 50s to \nlow 60s while overnight lows plummet into the 30s for most. The \nexception will be east of the I-95 corridor where low \ntemperatures stay in the low 40s. Frost is possible Friday and \nSaturday night. \n\nHigh pressure will continue to build southward into the region \nSunday through Tuesday. Dry conditions and seasonable \ntemperatures expected each day with light north to east winds. A\nbackdoor cold front could try to push into the region Tuesday \ninto Tuesday night, but will have very little to no moisture \nwith it to produce any precipitation. A surge of cooler \ntemperatures will follow behind the front for the day on \nWednesday.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /18Z THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nNorth winds continue today with terminals near the metros\ngusting 15 to 20 knots this afternoon. Winds become light\novernight before shifting to northeast on Friday. Winds blow 5\nto 10 knots on Friday before becoming light and variable\novernight. On Saturday, winds shift to easterly, remaining light\nthroughout the day. VFR conditions are expected each day. \n\nVFR conditions Sunday through Monday night. Winds light and variable \nthrough the period as high pressure sits overhead. Winds then\nturn out of the NNE on Tuesday AOB 10 knots for the most part. \n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nSmall Craft Advisory conditions continue across the Chesapeake\nBay and lower tidal potomac through tonight into Friday. Winds\nwill diminish in the northern Bay, but the middle Chesapeake \nBay waters will likely remain elevated at least for a portion \nof the afternoon. \n\nFriday evening through Saturday, light winds are expected \nacross the waters. The exception will be in the southern \nportions of the Chesapeake Bay where wind gusts near advisory \ncriteria, so that SCA may need to be extended in time. \n\nLight winds expected Sunday and Monday with high pressure\noverhead. However, by Tuesday winds will turn out of the NNE \nand increase a bit. It is possible that winds could approach SCA\ncriteria in channeling flow along the Chesapeake Bay. \n\n&&\n\n.TIDES/COASTAL FLOODING...\nElevated tide levels are expected through the weekend as we approach \nthe Full Moon on October 26, along with being in King Tide season \n(though we are already past the highest astronomical tides that were \nat the beginning of October). Sensitive locations are forecast to \nreach Action Stage during most of the high tide cycles this week, \nwith Annapolis, Solomons Island, Dahlgren, Straits Point, and \nAlexandria expected to reach minor over the next few cycles.\nNumerous Coastal Flood Advisories remain in effect for these\nareas, with extensions possible in some locations. The presence\nof northerly winds is likely to keep tidal flooding within \nMinor flood stage.\n\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...Coastal Flood Advisory until 7 PM EDT Friday for MDZ014.\n     Coastal Flood Advisory until 3 AM EDT Friday for MDZ016-018.\n     Coastal Flood Advisory from 10 PM this evening to 3 AM EDT \n     Friday for MDZ017.\nVA...Coastal Flood Advisory until 3 AM EDT Friday for VAZ057.\n     Coastal Flood Advisory until 8 PM EDT this evening for VAZ054.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory until 11 AM EDT Friday for ANZ530>532-\n     538>540.\n     Small Craft Advisory until 6 PM EDT Friday for ANZ533-534-537-\n     541>543.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...AVS/KLW/CJL\nAVIATION...AVS/KLW/CJL\nMARINE...AVS/KLW/CJL\n"},"forecast":{"t":1792696410,"days":{"2026-10-22":{"hi":67,"lo":46,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-23":{"hi":64,"lo":40,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-24":{"hi":64,"lo":42,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-25":{"hi":67,"lo":43,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-26":{"hi":70,"lo":50,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-27":{"hi":69,"lo":48,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-28":{"hi":65,"lo":50,"pop":3,"short":"Partly Sunny"}}},"grid":{"t0":1792695600,"n":48,"ceil":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"vis":[10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0],"spd":[8,7,7,6,6,5,5,5,5,5,5,6,6,6,7,7,6,6,7,8,8,8,7,7,7,6,6,5,4,4,3,3,3,2,2,1,1,1,2,2,2,3,3,3,4,4,4,4],"gst":[12,13,13,12,12,12,12,12,12,13,14,14,14,14,14,14,13,13,13,13,13,12,12,11,10,10,9,8,8,8,8,7,7,6,5,5,4,5,5,5